1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:07,196
Before we begin, turn your iPhone sideways to landscape so the app screens and captions are easier to see.

2
00:00:07,196 --> 00:00:13,991
If the screen does not rotate, turn off Portrait Orientation Lock in Control Center. Welcome to Gig Tax Pros.

3
00:00:13,991 --> 00:00:20,787
Start on Home to see your day and reach the tools you use most. The five tabs are Home,

4
00:00:20,787 --> 00:00:27,583
Offers, Go Home, Position, and Earnings. The menu opens your trips, money, account, alerts, and other tools. You can

5
00:00:27,583 --> 00:00:29,371
explore before connecting an account.

6
00:00:30,171 --> 00:00:36,428
While parked, tap Start a drive and choose the details for that trip. End the drive when you arrive,

7
00:00:36,428 --> 00:00:42,686
then review its mileage and classification. Trips keeps your saved history, and you can add a missed trip manually.

8
00:00:42,686 --> 00:00:45,650
Optional driving and expense reminders are controlled in Account.

9
00:00:46,450 --> 00:00:53,377
Use the Home shortcuts to add income or an expense. Enter the amount and category, and attach a receipt

10
00:00:53,377 --> 00:01:00,304
if you have one. The app can read a chosen receipt on your iPhone. Always review the suggested information

11
00:01:00,304 --> 00:01:05,773
before saving. The Money screen brings income, expenses, statement imports, and available bank connections together.

12
00:01:06,573 --> 00:01:12,771
Offers helps you review a job before deciding. Open the screenshot guide and follow the pink arrows. It shows

13
00:01:12,771 --> 00:01:18,969
which iPhone buttons to press, how to save the picture, and how to bring it into Gig Tax Pros.

14
00:01:18,969 --> 00:01:25,168
This DoorDash screen is a published example. The guide uses clearly stated practice costs and time, and never saves

15
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:27,125
a practice job to your records.

16
00:01:27,925 --> 00:01:34,796
For your own screenshot, choose its gig app, then select the picture from Photos. Review the pay, guaranteed amount,

17
00:01:34,796 --> 00:01:41,666
total working miles, time, and additional costs. A delivery deadline is not the whole trip duration. Include unpaid driving

18
00:01:41,666 --> 00:01:48,537
and waiting. Cancel if the picture is wrong, or save your corrected numbers. Your choice to accept a job

19
00:01:48,537 --> 00:01:50,345
stays in the gig app.

20
00:01:51,145 --> 00:01:57,882
Earnings shows results from the records you have saved. Open Goals to set daily, weekly, and hourly targets and

21
00:01:57,882 --> 00:02:04,618
your estimated vehicle cost per mile. These values affect offer estimates. Use costs that fit your vehicle, and remember

22
00:02:04,618 --> 00:02:09,227
that missing information can change the result. Sample views are marked as examples.

23
00:02:10,027 --> 00:02:16,906
Go Home helps you plan around an earnings goal, destination, and time to finish. Enter the full job and

24
00:02:16,906 --> 00:02:23,784
waiting time when comparing an offer. When you request route comparisons, check the pickup, drop-off, and onward trip. Review

25
00:02:23,784 --> 00:02:28,491
the estimates while parked; traffic and extra stops can change your arrival time.

26
00:02:29,291 --> 00:02:36,019
Position helps you explore waiting areas using your saved job history and destination. Choose your current location and destination

27
00:02:36,019 --> 00:02:42,746
before asking for comparisons. A new account may not have enough history yet. These are estimates from available records,

28
00:02:42,746 --> 00:02:45,579
not a promise that another gig will arrive.

29
00:02:46,379 --> 00:02:52,636
Tax and Goals is where you can ask questions about your recorded work and goals. Review the context shown

30
00:02:52,636 --> 00:02:58,892
with each answer. Tax details you choose to save need your confirmation. For filing decisions or questions about your

31
00:02:58,892 --> 00:03:01,855
situation, use Get help to reach your tax team.

32
00:03:02,655 --> 00:03:08,716
Ratings and reviews keeps the scores and feedback you choose to record for each gig platform. Add a rating

33
00:03:08,716 --> 00:03:14,776
snapshot or review, then look at the history and guidance. Leave customer names and private details out. These are

34
00:03:14,776 --> 00:03:19,241
your saved records; entering them does not change a rating in the gig platform.

35
00:03:20,041 --> 00:03:26,903
In Account, activate your tax team’s invitation and sign in with that client account. Review which phone records you

36
00:03:26,903 --> 00:03:33,765
want to copy and sync. Optional bank and work-account connections depend on your firm’s setup. Work-account updates are not

37
00:03:33,765 --> 00:03:39,183
a live feed of incoming offers. Account also contains privacy information and your reminder controls.

38
00:03:39,983 --> 00:03:46,775
Get help opens the office map. As approved locations join, they appear here without an app update. Use your

39
00:03:46,775 --> 00:03:53,568
location or ZIP code, check an office’s address and exterior photo, and use street view where available. Open driving

40
00:03:53,568 --> 00:04:00,360
directions in Apple Maps. Call the listed number or open its appointment link. A twenty-four-seven label appears only for

41
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:01,790
a confirmed staffed line.

42
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:08,680
Start with one real drive, income entry, or expense, and build your records as you work. Review anything read

43
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:14,770
from a picture before saving. You can replay this tour from Help and return to the interactive screenshot guide

44
00:04:14,770 --> 00:04:17,975
whenever you need it. Your next step starts on Home.
